{"id": "EUVD-2026-76543", "enisaUuid": "f1c265f4-0b1e-3132-b1eb-25f582586f89", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: reject a tree connect response whose byte count is too small\n\nCIFSTCon() bounds its strnlen() over the byte area with the server's\nByteCount minus two, which for ByteCount 0 or 1 goes negative as an int\nand converts to a huge size_t.  The later subtraction wraps the __u16\nbytes_left, and that is what bounds cifs_strndup_from_utf16(): a bound of\nup to 65535 against a ~16 KB cifs_req_poolp object runs off the end of the\nslab object, and the bytes reach userspace through tcon->nativeFileSystem\nin /proc/fs/cifs/DebugData.\n\nReject a byte area too small for what the parser consumes.  Two bytes is\nthe least it can consume, and no conformant response carries fewer.  The\nnew trace point is the 129th smb_eio_trace entry, which __mode(byte)\ncannot represent, so the attribute goes with it.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:45:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:48:03", "baseScore": 9.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d837645a719151ed392d4d9cab4571c2753dab12", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2ae219762ebac929bf6ab3473681f10ed566af08", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3be89e8039a85fa3b6cd5f9dcc4c1459eb356c2d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/411e484fe71a7f1028de617447edad9cb6d9d68a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/65deb18359341141d37dc86fc7853511be3c87a7"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89631", "GHSA-95qf-fgcq-pcrc"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.46, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "10923eca-cfdf-38fe-afff-f788dd983a47", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "292a25e2-0794-3a22-b6cc-b485cde164f0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cc20c031bb067eb3280a1c4b5c42295093e24863 <65deb18359341141d37dc86fc7853511be3c87a7"}, {"id": "4798eb13-51bb-3adc-b738-b7488e893c14", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.30"}, {"id": "593307c8-fcbc-3568-a818-7b2f5c844fb1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "595cab6b-11a5-359f-8821-eadc4e1dd787", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cc20c031bb067eb3280a1c4b5c42295093e24863 <2ae219762ebac929bf6ab3473681f10ed566af08"}, {"id": "7c603080-13dd-3739-8ff9-0a12b527b7f3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "a75dadd2-f7ff-31b4-8246-2cbaae50c29c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}, {"id": "d42cc5ae-be89-3962-8138-807634556323", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cc20c031bb067eb3280a1c4b5c42295093e24863 <3be89e8039a85fa3b6cd5f9dcc4c1459eb356c2d"}, {"id": "dea9f482-21b8-3328-b49d-1303723fbe54", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "dee33ebd-fdcb-3b18-bbd6-797a45c699c8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "e29f1007-ebb9-3a69-9129-0ecf1152938e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cc20c031bb067eb3280a1c4b5c42295093e24863 <411e484fe71a7f1028de617447edad9cb6d9d68a"}, {"id": "e32056cd-7e0f-3f84-8abd-d1b8fa9e650c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cc20c031bb067eb3280a1c4b5c42295093e24863 <d837645a719151ed392d4d9cab4571c2753dab12"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e597f4d8-0cab-342e-85c8-5b288c436493", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}